<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 5-yr govt bond yield rises to 15.78 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary 5-yr govt bond yield rises to 15.78 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on Hungary's five-year government bonds was set by auction at 15.78 percent, up from 15.65 percent set at an auction one month ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2002/F SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    July 24, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    June 24, 2002</p>
<p>    Total on offer			4,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received		11,575 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated		     4,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued			  4,400 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield		   15.78 pct</p>
<p>    Average price			    97.52 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum price			    97.90 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 14.00 percent, payable semi-annually starting from December 24, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
